  ],
  "og_image": "/assets/og/the-exception.png",
  "og_image_alt": "When Leaders Think the Rules Don’t Apply to Them: Entitlement begins when responsibility starts feeling like something everyone else should carry. TheWrkShop, Leadership & Culture.",
  "scriptures": [
    {
      "ref": "2 Samuel 11:1",
      "text": "In the spring, at the time when kings go off to war…. David remained in Jerusalem."
    },
    {
      "ref": "Deuteronomy 17:17",
      "text": "He must not take many wives, or his heart will be led astray."
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "the_revelation",
      "label": "The Revelation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "One of the most dangerous sentences available to a leader is:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "“THIS IS DIFFERENT.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "My situation is different.",
            "My pressure is different.",
            "My responsibility is different.",
            "My contribution is different.",
            "My needs are different."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Therefore:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "the boundary should bend.",
            "the policy shouldn’t apply.",
            "the normal accountability isn’t necessary."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Nobody announces:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“I am becoming entitled.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Instead:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "WE DEVELOP A REASON WHY OUR EXCEPTION MAKES SENSE."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "david_stayed_home",
      "label": "David Stayed Home",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "2 Samuel 11 begins quietly:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“…at the time when kings go off to war….”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Then:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“David remained in Jerusalem.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That doesn’t mean staying home itself caused everything that followed."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But Scripture intentionally sets the scene."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "David has reached enormous power."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Others go.",
            "David remains."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Then rooftop.",
            "Bathsheba.",
            "Inquiry.",
            "Taking.",
            "Cover-up.",
            "Uriah.",
            "Death."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The catastrophic acts come later."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But the story opens with a powerful king increasingly able to arrange reality around himself."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "POWER INCREASES YOUR ABILITY TO TURN DESIRE INTO ACCESS."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s why power requires deeper restraint."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_lie",
      "label": "The Lie",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“I’VE EARNED THIS.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "I’ve worked harder.",
            "Sacrificed more.",
            "Built this.",
            "Carried everyone.",
            "Taken the risk."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Therefore:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "I deserve…."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Be careful."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Because gratitude says:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“Look what I’ve been entrusted with.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Entitlement says:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "“LOOK WHAT I’M OWED.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Those are very different postures."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_truth",
      "label": "The Truth",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "THE MORE POWER YOU HAVE, THE LESS YOU CAN AFFORD TO BELIEVE NORMAL BOUNDARIES NO LONGER APPLY TO YOU."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Power means:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "more access.",
            "more resources.",
            "more opportunity.",
            "more people reluctant to say no."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Which means internal restraint becomes increasingly important."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The question isn’t:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“CAN I?”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "It is:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "“SHOULD I?”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "And:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "“WOULD I BELIEVE THIS WAS APPROPRIATE IF SOMEONE ELSE DID IT?”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s a powerful test."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_audit",
      "label": "The Audit",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullet_list",
          "items": [
            "WHERE HAVE I STARTED EXPECTING EXCEPTIONS?",
            "WHAT BOUNDARY NOW FEELS BENEATH ME?",
            "WHAT HAVE I BEGUN JUSTIFYING BECAUSE OF MY CONTRIBUTION?",
            "DO I HAVE ACCESS THAT MY CHARACTER HAS NOT LEARNED TO GOVERN?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Then:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "WHAT AM I CALLING PRIVILEGE THAT MAY ACTUALLY BE TEMPTATION?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_surrender",
      "label": "The Surrender",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Put the boundary back before you need it."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Don’t wait for desire to become crisis."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Remember:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "BOUNDARIES ARE NOT INSULTS TO YOUR MATURITY."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Sometimes they are evidence of it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "take_it_with_you",
      "label": "Take It With You",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "Power increases your ability to turn desire into access."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_prayer",
      "label": "The Prayer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Father,"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Expose entitlement in me."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Keep blessing from becoming permission.",
            "Keep access from becoming indulgence.",
            "Keep responsibility from becoming exemption."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Teach me to steward power by governing myself under Your authority."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "What You prohibit is not beneath me.",
            "What You command still applies to me."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Jesus is Lord."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "In Jesus name,",
            "Amen."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "hidden_gems",
      "label": "Hidden Gems 💎",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "We rarely announce entitlement. We develop reasons our exception makes sense."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Power increases your ability to turn desire into access."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Gratitude says, “Look what I’ve been entrusted with.” Entitlement says, “Look what I’m owed.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Do I have access my character has not learned to govern?"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Boundaries are not insults to maturity. Sometimes they are evidence of it."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "-TheWrkShop"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "__insert_block_header": "2026-10-28_2-samuel-11-1_the-exception|"
}
